        "content": "## 1. Insiemi, parametri e variabili decisionali\n\n### Insiemi\n- Centri:\n\\[\nI=\\{A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H\\}\n\\]\n- Zone:\n\\[\nJ=\\{Z1,Z2,\\ldots,Z10\\}\n\\]\n\n### Parametri\n- Costi di apertura:\n\\[\n(c_A,c_B,c_C,c_D,c_E,c_F,c_G,c_H)\n=(24,20,27,22,25,19,23,21)\n\\]\n- \\(a_{ji}=1\\) se il centro \\(i\\) copre la zona \\(j\\), \\(0\\) altrimenti.\n- Copertura minima richiesta:\n\\[\nr_j=\n\\begin{cases}\n2 & j\\in\\{Z3,Z7\\}\\\\\n1 & \\text{altrimenti}\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n- Numero massimo di centri apribili:\n\\[\nK=5\n\\]\n\n### Variabili decisionali\nPer ogni \\(i\\in I\\):\n\\[\nx_i=\n\\begin{cases}\n1 & \\text{se il centro }i\\text{ viene aperto}\\\\\n0 & \\text{altrimenti}\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nLe singole variabili sono denominate \\(x_A,x_B,\\ldots,x_H\\).\n\n## 2. Formulazione matematica completa\n\n### Funzione obiettivo\n\\[\n\\min\\ 24x_A+20x_B+27x_C+22x_D+25x_E+19x_F+23x_G+21x_H\n\\]\n\n### Vincoli di copertura\n\\[\nx_A+x_C\\geq 1 \\qquad &&\\text{(Z1)}\n\\]\n\\[\nx_A+x_B\\geq 1 &&\\text{(Z2)}\n\\]\n\\[\nx_A+x_B+x_D\\geq 2 &&\\text{(Z3)}\n\\]\n\\[\nx_B+x_E\\geq 1 &&\\text{(Z4)}\n\\]\n\\[\nx_B+x_C+x_F\\geq 1 &&\\text{(Z5)}\n\\]\n\\[\nx_C+x_D+x_G\\geq 1 &&\\text{(Z6)}\n\\]\n\\[\nx_D+x_E+x_H\\geq 2 &&\\text{(Z7)}\n\\]\n\\[\nx_E+x_F+x_H\\geq 1 &&\\text{(Z8)}\n\\]\n\\[\nx_F+x_G\\geq 1 &&\\text{(Z9)}\n\\]\n\\[\nx_G+x_H\\geq 1 &&\\text{(Z10)}\n\\]\n\n### Limite sul numero di centri\n\\[\nx_A+x_B+x_C+x_D+x_E+x_F+x_G+x_H\\leq 5\n\\]\n\n### Dominio\n\\[\nx_i\\in\\{0,1\\}\\qquad \\forall i\\in I\n\\]\n\n## 3. Codice Python con Gurobi\n\n```python\nimport gurobipy as gp\nfrom gurobipy import GRB\nimport json\n\ncentri = [\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\", \"E\", \"F\", \"G\", \"H\"]\nzone = [\"Z1\", \"Z2\", \"Z3\", \"Z4\", \"Z5\", \"Z6\", \"Z7\", \"Z8\", \"Z9\", \"Z10\"]\n\ncosti = {\n    \"A\": 24, \"B\": 20, \"C\": 27, \"D\": 22,\n    \"E\": 25, \"F\": 19, \"G\": 23, \"H\": 21\n}\n\nzone_coperte = {\n    \"A\": [\"Z1\", \"Z2\", \"Z3\"],\n    \"B\": [\"Z2\", \"Z3\", \"Z4\", \"Z5\"],\n    \"C\": [\"Z1\", \"Z5\", \"Z6\"],\n    \"D\": [\"Z3\", \"Z6\", \"Z7\"],\n    \"E\": [\"Z4\", \"Z7\", \"Z8\"],\n    \"F\": [\"Z5\", \"Z8\", \"Z9\"],\n    \"G\": [\"Z6\", \"Z9\", \"Z10\"],\n    \"H\": [\"Z7\", \"Z8\", \"Z10\"]\n}\n\ncopertura_richiesta = {\n    z: 2 if z in [\"Z3\", \"Z7\"] else 1\n    for z in zone\n}\n\nenv = gp.Env(empty=True)\nenv.setParam(\"OutputFlag\", 0)\nenv.start()\n\nmodel = gp.Model(\"copertura_zone\", env=env)\n\nx = {\n    i: model.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=\"x_\" + i)\n    for i in centri\n}\n\nmodel.setObjective(\n    gp.quicksum(costi[i] * x[i] for i in centri),\n    GRB.MINIMIZE\n)\n\nfor z in zone:\n    model.addConstr(\n        gp.quicksum(x[i] for i in centri if z in zone_coperte[i])\n        >= copertura_richiesta[z],\n        name=\"copertura_\" + z\n    )\n\nmodel.addConstr(\n    gp.quicksum(x[i] for i in centri) <= 5,\n    name=\"massimo_centri\"\n)\n\nmodel.optimize()\n\nstatus_names = {\n    1: \"LOADED\",\n    2: \"OPTIMAL\",\n    3: \"INFEASIBLE\",\n    4: \"INF_OR_UNBD\",\n    5: \"UNBOUNDED\",\n    6: \"CUTOFF\",\n    7: \"ITERATION_LIMIT\",\n    8: \"NODE_LIMIT\",\n    9: \"TIME_LIMIT\",\n    10: \"SOLUTION_LIMIT\",\n    11: \"INTERRUPTED\",\n    12: \"NUMERIC\",\n    13: \"SUBOPTIMAL\",\n    14: \"INPROGRESS\",\n    15: \"USER_OBJ_LIMIT\",\n    16: \"WORK_LIMIT\",\n    17: \"MEM_LIMIT\"\n}\n\nstatus = status_names.get(model.Status, \"STATUS_\" + str(model.Status))\n\nif model.Status == GRB.OPTIMAL:\n    result = {\n        \"status\": \"OPTIMAL\",\n        \"objective\": float(round(model.ObjVal, 10)),\n        \"variables\": {\n            \"x_\" + i: float(round(x[i].X))\n            for i in centri\n        }\n    }\nelse:\n    result = {\n        \"status\": status,\n        \"objective\": None,\n        \"variables\": {}\n    }\n\nmodel.dispose()\nenv.dispose()\n\nprint(\"SOLUTION_JSON=\" + json.dumps(result, separators=(\",\", \":\")))\n```\n\n## 4. Sintesi della soluzione\n\nIl modello ha stato **OPTIMAL** e valore ottimo:\n\n\\[\nz^*=106\n\\]\n\nI centri aperti sono:\n\n\\[\nx_A=x_B=x_D=x_F=x_H=1\n\\]\n\nmentre \\(C\\), \\(E\\) e \\(G\\) restano chiusi. Vengono quindi aperti esattamente cinque centri, garantendo doppia copertura sia a Z3 sia a Z7.",
